course: dictionary
lesson: 2673
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The same word can have more than one meaning. «Dial» is a good example. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. These words are its context, and they leave clues. «Turn the dial to make the music louder» tells you a dial is a round control that you turn.
explain: «Read the time on the dial» is about the round face of a clock, with numbers and a pointer. «Dial 999 in an emergency» is about pressing numbers to make a phone call. Ask: which meaning fits the sentence? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it makes sense.
explain: Some words change their form, too. «She dialled the number.» Dialled is the past of dial, so it means she pressed the numbers in the past. The clues are in the words around it.
fact: A dial is the round face of a clock, watch or measuring instrument, with numbers and a pointer.
fact: A dial is also a round control that you turn to change something, like the volume or the oven temperature.
fact: To dial a number means to press or turn the numbers to make a phone call.
fact: In an emergency you dial 999 (UK, Ireland), 911 (USA, Canada), 000 (Australia) or 111 (New Zealand).
fact: «Britain's speaking clock (dial 123) began in 1936»: here dial means to phone a number.
exercise: «The dial on the wall clock showed half past three.» What is a dial in this sentence? | A small bird that sings at dawn | *The round face of a clock, with numbers and a pointer | A phone call to a friend | To press numbers on a keypad
exercise: «Turn the dial to make the music louder.» What does dial mean here? | The pointer on a ruler | *A round control that you turn to change the volume | A clock tower in a town square | To phone someone long distance
exercise: «Nadia dialled 999 when she saw the smoke.» What does dialled mean? | *Pressed the numbers to make a phone call | Turned a round control to make it louder | Counted the steps on a scale | Read the time on a clock
test: «In the 1990s, families used a dial-up modem to reach the internet.» What does dial-up mean here, as a clue? | It is a kind of clock that ticks very loudly | It means a round volume control on a radio | *It connected through the phone line, which was slow | It means very fast and modern
test: Which sentence uses dial as a round control you turn? | «He dialled his gran's number at teatime.» | *«The dial on the oven shows the right heat.» | «The phone dials quickly when you press it.» | «She will dial down the music so we can talk.»
exam: In «The scale's dial shows 40 kilograms, so read where the pointer stops», what does dial mean? | *The round face with numbers and a pointer | A phone call made with numbers | A soft drink served cold | To press numbers to call someone
